GitHub account with repository access

Installed TaskCLI on your system

Personal Access Token (PAT) from GitHub with repo and workflow scopes

02
Configure GitHub Token
Link TaskCLI with your GitHub account using a PAT.

Terminal command

Generate a new PAT in GitHub

Copy the token securely

In TaskCLI, run:

bash
taskcli config set github.token YOUR_TOKEN
03
Set Repository Context
Define which repository TaskCLI should connect to.

Navigate to your project folder

Run:

bash
taskcli config set github.repo owner/repo-name
Verify with:

bash
taskcli config list
04
Link Tasks to Issues
Associate TaskCLI tasks with GitHub issues.

Create a new task:

bash
taskcli add "Fix login bug" --issue 42
